[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（英音）]
[ti:A Perfect Alibi]
[00:13.59]What was wrong with the man's story?
[00:19.20]'At the time the murder was committed I was travelling on the 8 o'clock train to London,' said the man.
[00:28.62]'Do you always catch such an early train?' asked the inspector.
[00:34.94]'Of course I do,' answered the man.
[00:38.80]'I must be at work at 10 o'clock.
[00:42.39]My employer will confirm that I was there on time.'
[00:48.09]'Would a later train get you to work on time?' asked the inspector.
[00:55.17]'I suppose it would, but I never catch a later train.'
[01:01.97]'At what time did you arrive at the station?'
[01:06.74]'At ten to eight. I bought a paper and waited for the train.'
[01:14.38]'And you didn't notice anything unusual?'
[01:19.52]'Of course not.'
[01:22.72]'I suggest,' said the inspector,' that you are not telling the truth.
[01:29.23]I suggest that you did not catch the 8 o'clock train,
[01:34.06]but that you caught the 8.25 which would still get you to work on time.
[01:41.02]You see, on the morning of the murder, the 8 o'clock train did not run at all.
[01:48.29]It broke down at Ferngreen station and was taken off the line.'
